// Small wild birds (Mariano, 2026-10-13: "Add butterflies and birds (small) in the
// environment, depending on climate", and "birds should be killable though, but drop
// nothing"). Each climate has its own: finches in meadows, thrushes in broadleaf woods,
// crossbills in the conifers, buntings on the tundra, larks in the desert, parakeets in the
// jungle, wagtails by fresh water and swallows over open country.
//
// They are `Flier`s (docs/creature-ai.md, "Movement styles"): they hop about the ground
// pecking, take wing to cross their range or when a player comes near, keep `fly` blocks
// over the land and the treetops in flight, and flutter down to land again. They count
// against a budget of their own near each player (`birds_near` in creatures.ron), so they
// never crowd out the animals on the ground. They drop nothing and give no Hunter
// experience: there is nothing to butcher.
(
    creatures: [
        (
